==English==
{{was wotd|2010|April|27}}
===Etymology===
From {{term|jynx|lang=en}} in the {{l/en|transferred sense}} “a charm or spell”.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK|US}} {{IPA|/dʒɪŋks/|lang=en}}
* {{a|US|also}} {{IPA|/dʒiːŋks/|lang=en}}
* {{homophones|jynx|lang=en}}
* {{rhymes|ɪŋks|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|jinxes}}

# A [[hex]]; an [[evil]] [[spell]].
# A person or thing supposed to bring [[bad luck]].

====Synonyms====
*  {{sense|hex}} [[curse]], [[hoodoo]], [[Indian sign]], [[spell]]

====Derived terms====
* [[reverse jinx]]

